  "model": "Siemens LMV5 burner management via BASgatewayLX",
  "short_model": "BASgatewayLX Siemens LMV5",
  "model_slug": "basgatewaylx-siemens-lmv5",
  "aliases": [
    "LMV5",
    "LMV51",
    "LMV52",
    "Siemens LMV5 Modbus",
    "AZL5"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Boiler burner management system",
  "applies_to": "Siemens LMV5 (LMV51/52) burner management systems with Modbus through the AZL5 display, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Siemens LMV5: 142 objects (85 AI, 31 AO, 26 BI), 60 polled by default. Inputs cover phase, every actuator position, VSD output, fuel type, output, setpoint and actual value, flame signal, throughput, O2 and efficiency (LMV52), counters and the current error, plus the input/output states. Program stop and the load-controller operating mode are polled outputs; Modbus local/remote, remote operating mode, external setpoint W3, preselected output and fuel selection are unpolled outputs.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Siemens_Combustion_Control_LMV5_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the LMV5 Modbus documentation (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/QSGSection_08_2011modbus.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 60 of the 142 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Siemens_Combustion_Control_LMV5_a",
    "doc_number": "Siemens_Combustion_Control_LMV5_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/SiemensCombustionControlLMV5.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set Modbus mode to remote and the remote operating mode, then write the external setpoint W3 (or a preselected output). Read phase, output, actual value and flame signal.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AO 61",
        "name": "Modbus mode: Local / Remote",
        "why": "Modbus mode: local or remote"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 63",
        "name": "Operating mode in Remote mode Auto Remote ON Remote OFF",
        "why": "Operating mode in remote (auto/on/off)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 64",
        "name": "External setpoint W3 Unit: See address 18 / 19",
        "why": "External setpoint W3"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Phase",
        "why": "Burner phase"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 11",
        "name": "Current output",
        "why": "Current output"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 12",
        "name": "Current setpoint / temperature / pressure",
        "why": "Current setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 13",
        "name": "Actual value / temperature / pressure Unit: See address 18 / 19",
        "why": "Actual temperature/pressure"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 14",
        "name": "Flame signal",
        "why": "Flame signal"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 45",
        "name": "Outputs Alarm",
        "why": "Alarm output"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 24",
        "name": "Current error: Error code",
        "why": "Current error code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Modbus mode (AO 61) must be remote before the remote operating mode (AO 63) and external setpoint W3 (AO 64) act; all three are unpolled in the published profile.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "The BASgatewayLX presents each Modbus device as its own virtual BACnet device on BACnet IP; give it a unique device instance and Modbus address (serial) or IP address (Modbus TCP) when you add it with this profile.",
      "One BASgatewayLX handles up to 100 Modbus devices and 1000 polled points in total, so leave unneeded rows unpolled."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Modbus downtime (AO 62) sets how long the LMV5 waits before dropping back to local after communication stops.",
      "Unpolled rows do not appear as BACnet objects until enabled in the gateway's device profile page."
    ]
  },
